course: dictionary
lesson: 2666
title: Dewy: wet, fresh and soft
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one the writer means. Look at the clues. «Look at a garden spider in the middle of its web on a dewy autumn morning» tells you the morning is cool and early, and dewy means wet with dew: the tiny drops of water on grass and leaves.
explain: Dewy can also mean fresh, soft and slightly shiny, as in dewy skin. Dewy-eyed is different again: it means eyes wet with tears, or someone who is too hopeful and innocent. Ask yourself: what does the rest of the sentence tell me? The clues will tell you which meaning fits.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. If you swap in «wet with dew» for dewy in the spider sentence and it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Dewy means wet with dew.
fact: Dew is tiny drops of water that form on grass and leaves on cool nights.
fact: «Dewy» can also mean fresh, soft and slightly shiny.
fact: «Dewy-eyed» means with eyes wet with tears, or too hopeful and innocent.
fact: In science, dew shows that water vapour in the air has cooled and turned into liquid on cold surfaces.
exercise: «Look at a garden spider in the middle of its web on a dewy autumn morning.» What does dewy mean in this sentence? | *Wet with tiny drops of water | Loud and noisy | Dry and dusty | Hot and sunny
exercise: Mia is dewy-eyed as she waves goodbye to her gran. What does dewy-eyed suggest? | *Her eyes are wet with tears, and she feels soft and emotional | Her eyes are bright red from the sun | Her eyes are closed and sleepy | Her eyes can see far away
exercise: «Look at a garden spider in the middle of its web on a dewy autumn morning: dry spokes, a sticky spiral, and the spider walking on the dry lines.» Find and copy one word that means the opposite of wet. | *dry | spider | spiral | sticky
test: What forms on grass and leaves on cool nights, making them dewy? | Sunshine | Hail | Rain | *Dew
test: What does dewy most likely mean in the phrase dewy skin? | Cold and frozen | *Fresh, soft and slightly shiny | Very old and wrinkled | Covered in mud
exam: In a story, what does a dewy morning usually set? | A hot afternoon at the beach | A loud, busy rush hour | *A calm, fresh, early scene | A night of thunder
